# 10. Menu and pricing operations

## 10.1 Price update flow

Merchant says:

> Change the family meal to $25.

The bot should reply:

> I found **Family Meal**. Current price: **$24.00**. New price: **$25.00**. Should I apply this now?

Buttons:

```text
Apply price
Cancel
```

On confirmation:

1. validate merchant permission;
2. write an audit event;
3. update the current menu price;
4. preserve existing confirmed order prices;
5. update future campaign eligibility;
6. invalidate stale menu cache;
7. notify any active campaign owner if the offer is affected.

## 10.2 Out-of-stock flow

Merchant says:

```text
The chicken shawarma is out
خلص الشاورما
```

The bot should ask:

```text
Out of stock until:
Today
A specific time
Until I turn it back on
```

Then:

- mark item unavailable;
- remove it from new recommendations;
- update menu immediately;
- identify affected pending orders;
- offer approved substitutions to customers;
- pause campaigns that depend on the item.

## 10.3 Opening-hours flow

Support:

```text
Open today until 10
Closed tomorrow
Pause orders for 45 minutes
We are open for pickup but not delivery
```

Separate:

```text
business_open
accepts_orders
accepts_delivery
accepts_pickup
paused_until
holiday_closure
```

Changing business hours should not automatically cancel already accepted orders. It should trigger an operational review.

## 10.4 AI menu import

Allow merchants to upload:

- PDF menu;
- image;
- spreadsheet;
- website link;
- text message.

The AI can extract candidate items, but the merchant must review:

- item name;
- price;
- options;
- ingredients;
- allergens;
- availability.

Never publish AI-extracted prices without merchant confirmation.

