# 11. Merchant broadcasts and paid campaigns

## 11.1 Campaign access gate

A merchant can create a paid campaign only when:

- Level 3 campaign-enabled;
- marketing terms accepted;
- sufficient balance or approved payment intent;
- valid menu and offer;
- audience consent available;
- no active quality suspension;
- order capacity is sufficient.

## 11.2 Campaign creation through merchant number

Example:

> Create a campaign for customers near Baakline who ordered shawarma more than 30 days ago. Offer a family meal for $24 this weekend.

The bot should respond with a structured preview:

```text
Objective: Reactivate inactive customers
Audience: 184 eligible opted-in customers
Offer: Family Meal
Price: $24.00
Validity: Friday–Sunday
Estimated message cost: $X.XX
Estimated total: $X.XX
Test batch: 20 customers
```

Buttons:

```text
Preview copy
Change audience
Change offer
Schedule test
Cancel
```

Final send requires a separate explicit confirmation.

## 11.3 Campaign safety

The AI cannot:

- add customers who opted out;
- invent a discount;
- hide campaign cost;
- use unverified menu prices;
- target sensitive attributes;
- send without the campaign gate;
- continue after a kill rule triggers.

## 11.4 Merchant campaign controls

Merchant commands:

```text
Pause campaign
Stop campaign
Show results
How much did I spend?
Which offer converted?
Recharge balance
```

A stop command should take effect immediately for unsent recipients.

