# 13. Ownership transfer, staff, and disputes

## 13.1 Add team member

Owner says:

> Add my manager Samir to the business account.

Flow:

1. owner chooses role;
2. enters manager phone;
3. manager receives invite;
4. manager accepts;
5. owner or admin confirms;
6. membership becomes active.

## 13.2 Role permissions

| Role | Profile | Menu | Orders | Campaigns | Billing | Team |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Owner | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Manager | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Limited | No |
| Kitchen operator | No | Stock only | Yes | No | No | No |
| Marketing manager | No | Offer items | No | Yes | No | No |
| Finance user | No | No | Read-only | Read-only | Yes | No |

## 13.3 Ownership dispute

If two people claim the same business:

- freeze sensitive changes;
- keep the public listing visible;
- preserve existing verified owner access unless there is a security incident;
- notify both parties that a review is required;
- request independent proof;
- record all evidence;
- use a human decision;
- offer appeal.

Do not resolve ownership by whichever person replies fastest or uploads the best-looking screenshot.

## 13.4 Business closed or sold

Support:

```text
Temporarily closed
Permanently closed
New owner
Moved location
Duplicate page
```

Require evidence before deleting or transferring a verified profile.

