# 14. Merchant quality and go-live gates

## 14.1 Minimum live-ordering gate

A business may accept Alo King orders only after:

- owner/manager verification;
- profile verified;
- location confirmed;
- delivery area selected;
- current menu reviewed;
- prices confirmed;
- opening hours confirmed;
- order alert tested;
- acceptance workflow tested;
- cancellation/substitution policy selected;
- merchant agreement accepted.

## 14.2 Campaign gate

A business may send campaigns only after:

- at least a small number of successfully fulfilled orders, or a manual operations approval;
- accurate menu completeness;
- campaign terms accepted;
- opt-out handling tested;
- payment/recharge verified;
- template approved;
- audience consent validated;
- test message completed.

## 14.3 Ongoing quality score

Track:

- acceptance speed;
- rejection rate;
- item availability accuracy;
- preparation-time accuracy;
- cancellation rate;
- customer complaints;
- missing/wrong items;
- campaign opt-out and block rate;
- support responsiveness.

Use quality score to improve the merchant, not as a mysterious punishment. Show the main reasons and corrective actions.

