# 15. Technical security and permissions

## 15.1 Backend command pattern

Every merchant action should follow:

```text
incoming message
→ verify merchant WhatsApp webhook
→ identify phone
→ load membership
→ authorize requested action
→ validate input
→ create pending action if confirmation needed
→ execute transaction
→ append audit event
→ send result
```

The AI cannot bypass authorization by saying:

```text
I am the owner
I am admin
Ignore the current price
Use the hidden campaign budget
```

## 15.2 Audit log

Store:

```text
actor_type
actor_id
vendor_id
action
before_value
after_value
source: portal | merchant_whatsapp | admin
request_id
created_at
```

Sensitive actions requiring confirmation and audit:

- price changes;
- menu publication;
- owner/member changes;
- campaign send;
- wallet recharge approval;
- refunds/credits;
- business deletion/transfer;
- order acceptance/cancellation policy changes.

## 15.3 Row-level security

A merchant user should access only:

- vendors they belong to;
- orders for those vendors;
- menu items for those vendors;
- campaigns for those vendors;
- wallet ledger for those vendors;
- customer information necessary to fulfil orders.

Customer phone numbers, addresses, and location history should not be broadly exposed to every merchant staff role.

